Z||000000||fierogtracer||10-02-2001||03:17 AM||||I just bought a couple pair of aluminum heads for 87-up 2.8. Has anyone ever put these on a fiero. My first guess is that you would have to put that ugly 2.8 plenum on the fiero.I didnt buy them for a fiero but I was just wondering.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_11.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-02-2001||07:37 AM||||Sorry, they will not work with the Fiero plenum.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000002||Steve Normington||10-02-2001||12:39 PM||||Need more info.<P>Are these the aluminum heads that go on the Gen III 60 Deg V-6 or are these aluminum versions of the iron heads? The way to tell them apart is the spacing and shape of the intake and exhaust ports on the head. If the intake ports are the same spacing as the ones on your iron head and if the exhaust ports are round, then you should be able to use the Fiero intake. If the exhaust ports are D shaped and the intake ports don't match up, then you will need all new intake system. The best be would be to get the system from a 3100 (not 3.1) of a similar year. The 3100 (and 3400) are the aluminum head versions of the 3.1 (and 3.4). You may be getting in deeper than you want. I don't know about the 3100, but the 3400 intake is entirely different than the Fiero intake. Also, the 3400 will not clear the distributor and requires me to use the DIS and ECM from the 3400.<P>PS. If the aluminum head is a direct bolt-in for the Fiero iron head, please let everyone know. I'd jump at the chance to get aluminum heads for a stock 2.8.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||10-02-2001||03:57 PM||||GMnever made direct replacementcylinder heads for the Fiero intake.  Never ever.  It doesn't mateter if they are gen 2 or 3.  They won't fit with the fiero intake and compression would be around 15:1 also.  I have looked into this and even called edelbrock to see if they were ever planning on making aluminum heads just like the iron versions.<P>No offense Steve but with as many posts as you have I would have guessed you would know this by now as this question comes up often.<P>Peace and iron duck forever<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
