Z||000005||Steve Normington||10-03-2001||02:05 PM||||Must... defend... self.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B>I have looked into this and even called edelbrock to see if they were ever planning on making aluminum heads just like the iron versions.<P>No offense Steve but with as many posts as you have I would have guessed you would know this by now as this question comes up often.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I have heard the question if the Gen III heads will work with the 2.8 engine before. This question stated that the heads were for a 2.8. Since (to the best of my knowledge) the Gen III heads only came with 3100 and 3400's, I thought that these heads might be direct bolt ins for the 2.8 iron heads (like the ones you called Edelbrock about).<P>PS. I challange you to a key lime pie duel.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||10-03-2001||04:42 PM||||The gen 3 heads can be used on the Fiero engine but you have to use the Gen 3 intake as well cause the intake ports are spaced differently between the gen 2 and gen 3 aluminum head and the iron head.  Both gen 2 and gen 3 have the same size CC so they can be used with a 2.8 or a 3.1 engine.  Just have to use the proper pistons.<P>if you sue the gen 2 or 3 intake you have to use the computer as well cause they don't use a distributor and all that otehr good stuff that can be found in past threads.<P>I called Edelbrock to see if they were going to make heads with the intake ports set up like the fiero or iron head intake ports.  They said they weren't planning on making any kind of an aluminum head for any V6 head anytime soon.  They are staying with V8 heads.<P>Steve Meet me in Key west for that key lime pie duel and we can have a go at it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I hear they have good key lime pie there.||||reg||1
